<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    What leaves this device when the OS, rather than the person, copies app data.

    PRIVACY.md says "android:allowBackup=false is set, so the OS won't copy your data into
    cloud/adb backups". That attribute alone stopped being the whole answer at Android 12: it still
    turns off cloud backup and adb backup, but the documented note on `android:allowBackup` is that
    it does NOT disable device-to-device transfer. The app targets SDK 35, so on any phone running
    12 or later the D2D channel was governed by the platform default — copy everything — rather
    than by anything this project had written down. A person moving to a new handset would have had
    the journal, the photos and the safety plan carried across by the setup wizard, which is not
    what the privacy statement told them.

    So both channels are named here and both exclude everything. There are no <include> rules and
    there must not be any: this file is a deny-list only by virtue of listing every domain the app
    can write to, so a domain omitted here is a domain the platform default copies.

    `root` covers the app's internal storage — files/ (photos), databases/ (the journal) and
    shared_prefs/ (the PIN hash). `device_root` and `external` cover storage nothing in the app
    uses today; they are listed so that the day something does start writing there, it is excluded
    already rather than exported until someone remembers this file.

    Nothing here replaces `android:allowBackup="false"`, which stays in the manifest: this resource
    is only read on API 31+, and below that the attribute is what turns backup off.

    The person's own exports (Settings -> Backup) are unaffected — those are a file they choose to
    write, which is the only way data is meant to leave.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="device_root" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <device-transfer>
        <exclude domain="root" />
        <exclude domain="device_root" />
        <exclude domain="external" />
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
